### AJAX Controllers - Getting Translations for Current Language

**✅ CORRECT:**
```php
// Controllers/YourAjaxController.php
namespace Okay\Modules\YourModule\Controllers;

use Okay\Controllers\AbstractController;
use Okay\Core\Languages;
use Okay\Entities\TranslationsEntity;

class YourAjaxController extends AbstractController
{
    public function ajaxMethod(
        Languages $languages,
        TranslationsEntity $translationsEntity
    ) {
        // Determine language from referrer (AJAX requests may not have language prefix)
        $currentLangLabel = null;
        
        if (!empty($_SERVER['HTTP_REFERER'])) {
            $referer = $_SERVER['HTTP_REFERER'];
            if (preg_match('#/([a-z]{2})(/|$)#', $referer, $matches)) {
                $refererLangLabel = $matches[1];
                $allLanguages = $languages->getAllLanguages();
                foreach ($allLanguages as $lang) {
                    if ($lang->label === $refererLangLabel) {
                        $languages->setLangId($lang->id);
                        $currentLangLabel = $refererLangLabel;
                        break;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        
        // Fallback to $this->language or Languages
        if (empty($currentLangLabel)) {
            if (!empty($this->language)) {
                $currentLangLabel = $this->language->label;
            } else {
                $currentLangLabel = $languages->getLangLabel();
            }
        }
        
        // Load translations for current language (includes module translations)
        $translations = $translationsEntity->find(['lang' => $currentLangLabel, 'force' => true]);
        
        // Get translation value
        $errorMsg = isset($translations['module__error']) 
            ? (is_object($translations['module__error']) && isset($translations['module__error']->value)
                ? $translations['module__error']->value
                : (is_string($translations['module__error']) ? $translations['module__error'] : 'Error'))
            : 'Error';
        
        // Replace variables in translation
        $errorMsg = str_replace('{$variable}', $value, $errorMsg);
        
        return $this->response->setContent(json_encode(['message' => $errorMsg]), RESPONSE_JSON);
    }
}
```

**Rule**:
- **Always determine language from referrer** for AJAX controllers - referrer contains language prefix from current page URL
- **Use `TranslationsEntity::find(['lang' => $langLabel, 'force' => true])`** to load translations (automatically includes module translations)
- **Don't use `FrontTranslations::init()`** in AJAX controllers - it may use cached language
- **Access translation values**: `$translations['key']->value` (result is array of objects with `value` property)

