## Database Migrations Best Practices

### Creating New Entity Tables

**✅ CORRECT:**
```php
public function install()
{
    $this->migrateEntityTable(YourEntity::class, [
        (new EntityField('id'))
            ->setIndexPrimaryKey()
            ->setTypeInt(11, false)
            ->setAutoIncrement(),
        (new EntityField('name'))
            ->setTypeVarchar(255)
            ->setIsLang(), // For multilingual fields
        (new EntityField('visible'))
            ->setTypeTinyInt(1),
        (new EntityField('position'))
            ->setTypeInt(11),
    ]);
}
```

### Adding Fields to Existing Entities

**✅ CORRECT:**
```php
public function install()
{
    $this->migrateEntityField(
        VariantsEntity::class,
        (new EntityField('volume'))
            ->setTypeDecimal('10,5')
            ->setNullable() // If field can be NULL
    );
}

public function init()
{
    // REQUIRED: Register field for Entity queries
    $this->registerEntityField(VariantsEntity::class, 'volume');
}
```

### Composite Indexes

**✅ CORRECT:**
```php
$cityIdField = (new EntityField('city_id'))->setTypeVarchar(255, true);

$this->migrateEntityTable(YourEntity::class, [
    (new EntityField('id'))
        ->setIndexPrimaryKey()
        ->setTypeInt(11, false)
        ->setAutoIncrement(),
    (new EntityField('order_id'))
        ->setTypeInt(11)
        ->setIndex(null, $cityIdField), // Composite index
    $cityIdField,
