## Cron Tasks (Scheduler)

**✅ CORRECT:**
```php
use Okay\Core\Scheduler\Schedule;

public function init()
{
    $this->registerSchedule(
        (new Schedule([YourHelper::class, 'cronMethod']))
            ->name('Task description')
            ->time('0 0 * * *') // Cron expression
            ->overlap(false) // Prevent overlapping executions
            ->timeout(3600) // Timeout in seconds
    );
}
```

**Rule**: Use `Schedule` class for cron tasks. Method must be static or accessible via class name.

## Testing Checklist

Before deploying a module:

- [ ] All extenders with dependencies are registered in `services.php`
- [ ] Chain extensions return the object parameter
- [ ] No manual `serialize()`/`unserialize()` with `Settings`
- [ ] Validation only runs during checkout (check `checkout` parameter)
- [ ] Module gracefully handles empty/zero configuration (early returns)
- [ ] AJAX operations work correctly (test add-to-cart, update cart)
- [ ] No fatal errors in PHP error logs
- [ ] Entity fields added via `migrateEntityField()` are registered in `init()`
- [ ] Extender methods follow 1+N argument pattern
- [ ] Language keys use proper prefix pattern (`vendor__module__key`)
- [ ] Backend controllers registered and permissions set
- [ ] Template blocks registered if needed
- [ ] Database migrations tested (install/update methods)
- [ ] JavaScript files placed in `design/html/` (not `design/js/`) for `addFrontBlock()`
- [ ] Frontend controller routes use full namespace with `::class`
- [ ] AJAX controllers determine language from referrer, not from session
- [ ] AJAX controllers use `TranslationsEntity::find()` with `force=true` for translations
- [ ] Backend pages follow standard OkayCMS design structure
- [ ] All backend text is localized via `$btr->`
- [ ] Backend uses predefined CSS classes from `okay.css`
- [ ] Backend includes page title, description, settings block, and Apply button
- [ ] Module version follows semantic versioning (MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH)
- [ ] `module.json` contains required fields: version, vendor.email, vendor.site
- [ ] Template modifications (if any) are defined in `module.json` modifications section
- [ ] Smarty plugins (if any) are registered in `Init/SmartyPlugins.php`
- [ ] CSS/JS files are registered in `design/css.php` and `design/js.php`
- [ ] Payment/Delivery modules have `settings.xml` file
- [ ] Module preview image (preview.*) is provided (optional but recommended)

## Naming Conventions

### Module Structure
- **Namespace**: `Okay\Modules\Vendor\ModuleName`
- **Directory**: `Okay/Modules/Vendor/ModuleName/`
- **Extenders**: `Extenders/FrontExtender.php`, `Extenders/BackendExtender.php`
- **Entities**: `Entities/YourEntity.php` (must extend `Okay\Core\Entity\Entity`)
- **Helpers**: `Helpers/YourHelper.php` (must end with `Helper` suffix)
- **Controllers**: 
  - Frontend: `Controllers/YourController.php`
  - Backend: `Backend/Controllers/YourAdmin.php`

### Permission Names
**✅ CORRECT:**
```php
// Format: vendor__module__permission_name
const PERMISSION = 'maxit__min_order_amount'; // Double underscore
$this->addPermission('maxit__min_order_amount');
```

**Rule**: Permission names follow the same naming pattern: `vendor__module__permission_name` (double underscore between parts)

### Language Keys
**✅ CORRECT:**
```php
// In language files - format: vendor__module__variable_name
$lang['maxit__min_order__error'] = 'Error message';
$lang['maxit__min_order__error_title'] = 'Error';
$lang['maxit__min_order__title'] = 'Module Title';

// In templates
{$lang->maxit__min_order__error}
{$lang->maxit__min_order__error_title}
```

**❌ WRONG:**
```php
